  "overview": {
    "description": "TÃ¼bingen Tarock is a historical 4-player German tarot game, a version of Tarok-Quadrille documented by Guntram Kommerell from a variant played by students in TÃ¼bingen around 1890. Four players use a 78-card French-suited pack (21 numbered tarocks, Fool/Ski, 14 cards per suit with Cavalier). Play is counter-clockwise. After deal the dealer discards two cards; then either a player bids Raus (solo vs three) or in Rufen the dealer or others call a Kingâ€”the holder is the caller's secret partner. Total card value 91 points; teams count to 23 then again; declarer's side wins by scoring more than half of the remaining 45. Bonuses (Strafen) for families, kingdoms, tarock sequences, pagÃ¡t last trick.",
