    "origins": "Version of Tarok-Quadrille previously thought extinct in Germany by mid-19th century. Tarot in Germany dates to early 18th century; 4-player Quadrille-style (call a King for partner) appeared late 18th century. Guntram Kommerell learned it in the 1940s from his grandfather Otto, who grew up in CafÃ© Kommerell in TÃ¼bingen (student bar, c.1890). Variant passed down orally in the Kommerell family.",
